      "imageHeight": 266,
      "story": "War and Peace is a mural diptych by Brazilian painter Candido Portinari, created between 1952 and 1956 and presented by the Brazilian government to the United Nations (UN) in 1957. The two panels occupy opposite walls in the delegates' lobby of the General Assembly Building at United Nations Headquarters in New York City. Each composition measures approximately 14 by 10 m.",
      "facts": [
